From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: sun8i-emac: add the A733 GMAC200 with its per-channel interrupts

The A733 (sun60iw2) GMAC0 is the GMAC200 glue the A523 has, around a DWC
Ethernet QoS 5.30 core (MAC_VERSION 0x2053, read on silicon). The DT has named it
"allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200", "snps,dwmac-5.30a" since
arm64-dts-a733-add-gmac0-ethernet, but no binding described that
compatible. This one does:

- compatible: "allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200" with the "snps,dwmac-5.30a"
  fallback, also added to the select list.
- clocks, clock-names and tx/rx-internal-delay-ps as on the A523, whose
  glue it shares. power-domains stays required for the A523 only; the A733
  node has none. The A523's own constraints are unchanged, only split
  across two if-blocks.
- interrupts: either "macirq" alone, or "macirq", "tx-queue-0", "rx-queue-0".
  The two extra lines are GMAC0_PERCH_TX_0 and GMAC0_PERCH_RX_0 (A733 User
  Manual, Table 12-1). The form follows nxp,s32-dwmac.yaml upstream, commit
  cc7a3435dfad ("dt-bindings: net: nxp,s32-dwmac: Declare per-queue
  interrupts"), and the names are the ones snps,dwmac.yaml already defines.
  Both lines or neither: the glue selects multi-IRQ mode only with both
  (net-stmmac-dwmac-sun55i-per-channel-irqs).
- Every other compatible in this file keeps exactly one "macirq".

Left open, not decided here:
- The compatible's name. The tree's other A733 compatibles read
  "allwinner,sun60i-a733-*"; this one follows the vendor's "sun60iw2".
  Renaming it touches the driver match and the DT as well, so it is a
  change of its own; this patch documents the string the tree uses.
- The glue's syscon node, "allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac-syscon", is still
  undocumented.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-emac.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-emac.yaml
index fc62fb2a6..19a3b1a4f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-emac.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/allwinner,sun8i-a83t-emac.yaml
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ select:
           - allwinner,sun8i-v3s-emac
           - allwinner,sun50i-a64-emac
           - allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200
+          - allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200
   required:
     - compatible
 
@@ -44,15 +45,25 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - const: allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200
           - const: snps,dwmac-4.20a
+      - items:
+          - const: allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200
+          - const: snps,dwmac-5.30a
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
   interrupts:
-    maxItems: 1
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 3
 
   interrupt-names:
-    const: macirq
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: macirq
+      - items:
+          - const: macirq
+          - const: tx-queue-0
+          - const: rx-queue-0
 
   clocks:
     minItems: 1
@@ -220,7 +231,9 @@ allOf:
       properties:
         compatible:
           contains:
-            const: allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200
+            enum:
+              - allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200
+              - allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200
     then:
       properties:
         clocks:
@@ -241,8 +254,6 @@ allOf:
           multipleOf: 100
           description:
             External RGMII PHY TX clock delay chain value in ps.
-      required:
-        - power-domains
     else:
       properties:
         clocks:
@@ -251,6 +262,27 @@ allOf:
           maxItems: 1
         power-domains: false
 
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: allwinner,sun55i-a523-gmac200
+    then:
+      required:
+        - power-domains
+
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              const: allwinner,sun60iw2-gmac200
+    then:
+      properties:
+        interrupts:
+          maxItems: 1
+        interrupt-names:
+          maxItems: 1
 
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
